  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation and Adaptive Reuse of the Late 19th-Century &quot;Alte Feste&quot; Military Fort in Windhoek</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The oldest extant building in Windhoek, the late 19th-century Alte Feste has served many functions, from military fort during the German colonial period to national museum in the early 21st century. This project involves the stabilization, conservation, and adaptation of the building for reuse as a community cultural center.</narrative>
  </description>
